Subject: Exclude unavailable web seeds from the connection candidate budget
Base: libtorrent v2.0.15
Base-Commit: 1eb18faeae156d8dbbab42935c082f8b81f50989
Base-Blob: src/torrent.cpp 9c617fa842ff96a20713045813bee0dc2a2e0b60

A single-file HTTP redirect marks its original source as having no files,
but the source can remain interesting. maybe_connect_web_seeds() currently
counts that source against max_web_seed_connections before connect_web_seed()
rejects its all-false have_files bitmap. Three retained redirect origins can
exhaust the default budget and prevent the healthy target from being visited.

Skip a nonempty all-false have_files bitmap before decrementing the budget.
An empty bitmap still means all files are available. Sources with some files
remain eligible, and active or resolving eligible sources still consume a
connection slot. No connection limit, HTTP policy, DNS delay, ban or retry
state is changed.

Runtime regression: the owned loopback test run_redirect_chain.py follows
three HTTP 302 origins to a healthy final server, alongside an original
HTTP 404 source. Stock and diagnostic 5.2.4 stall without ever requesting
the final server. A corrected build must complete with the expected SHA256.

diff --git a/src/torrent.cpp b/src/torrent.cpp
--- a/src/torrent.cpp
+++ b/src/torrent.cpp
@@ -10630,7 +10630,9 @@ void torrent::maybe_connect_web_seeds()
 		{
 			auto const w = i++;
-			if (w->disabled || w->removed || w->retry > now || !w->interesting)
+			// Seeds with no files left must not consume connection slots.
+			if (w->disabled || w->removed || w->retry > now || !w->interesting
+				|| (!w->have_files.empty() && w->have_files.none_set()))
 				continue;
 
 			--limit;
 			if (w->peer_info.connection || w->resolving)
